{"step_index":186,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T18:50:11Z","thinking":"**Clarifying Deployment Options**\n\nOkay, so I'm digging into the difference between Expo Go and development builds for this project. The client specifically asked about a development build after testing/debugging is complete. I'm focusing on clarifying how Expo Go works for prototyping, versus what's necessary for deployment. It sounds like they're aware of the limitations, so I'm going to start from there.\n\n\n**Differentiating Build Methods**\n\nI'm now clarifying the distinctions between `expo-dev-client` and production builds using `eas build`. Specifically, the critical point is that Expo Go serves as a prototyping environment. It doesn't allow for custom native code, or submission to the App Store. On the other hand, the development build, created via `npx eas build`, incorporates the intended app ID, icon, and splash screen, along with custom native modules, producing a real native app.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"{\\n  \\\"cli\\\": {\\n    \\\"version\\\": \\\">= 14.0.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"build\\\": {\\n    \\\"development\\\": {\\n      \\\"developmentClient\\\": true,\\n      \\\"distribution\\\": \\\"internal\\\",\\n      \\\"ios\\\": {\\n        \\\"simulator\\\": false\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"preview\\\": {\\n      \\\"distribution\\\": \\\"internal\\\",\\n      \\\"ios\\\": {\\n        \\\"simulator\\\": false\\n      },\\n      \\\"android\\\": {\\n        \\\"buildType\\\": \\\"apk\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"production\\\": {\\n      \\\"ios\\\": {\\n        \\\"simulator\\\": false\\n      },\\n      \\\"android\\\": {\\n        \\\"buildType\\\": \\\"app-bundle\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"submit\\\": {\\n    \\\"production\\\": {}\\n  }\\n}\\n\"","Description":"\"Create eas.json build configuration for development, preview, and production builds\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\brorm\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\snap-dialer\\\\eas.json\"","toolAction":"\"Writing eas.json\"","toolSummary":"\"Write eas.json configuration\""}}]}
